---

## ✨ Overview

Bring **Dolby Atmos**, **Spatializer**, **Game DAP**, and **Codec2 hardware/software audio decoding** (`AC-3`, `E-AC-3`, `E-AC-3 JOC`, and `AC-4`) to your Android build—paired with an expressive **Material 3** user interface.

| Module | Component | Library / Service |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Dolby DAP** | Hardware Audio Processing | `libhwdapaidl.so` |
| **Volume Leveler** | Dynamic Volume Listener | `libdlbvolaidl.so` |
| **Spatializer** | Immersive Spatial Audio | `libswspatializeraidl.so` |
| **Game DAP** | Low-Latency Gaming Profile | `libswgamedapaidl.so` |
| **Codec2 Decoders** | AC-3 / E-AC-3 / JOC / AC-4 | `media_codecs_dolby_audio.xml` |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Register Dolby Media Codecs
Ensure your device supports **Codec2** (`C2`), then include the Dolby codec definitions inside your vendor media codecs configuration (`media_codecs_c2.xml` or `media_codecs.xml`):

```xml
<Include href="media_codecs_dolby_audio.xml"/>
```

### 2. Inherit Dolby in Device Tree
Add the Dolby product makefile to your device's `device.mk`:

```makefile
\$(call inherit-product, hardware/dolby/dolby.mk)
```

### 3. Preserve VINTF Manifest & Compatibility Matrix
Do **not** overwrite VINTF manifest or matrix variables in your `BoardConfig.mk`—append to them with `+=` so the AIDL HAL entries from `hardware/dolby` remain intact:

```makefile
# ❌ Avoid overwriting with :=
# DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE := ...
# DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE := ...

# ✅ Append with += instead
DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE += ...
DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE += ...
```

---

## 🎛️ Audio Effects Configuration

Add the AIDL libraries, effects, and postprocess stream rules to your device's `audio_effects_config.xml`:

<details open>
<summary><strong>1. Libraries (<code>&lt;libraries&gt;</code>)</strong></summary>

```xml
<!-- DOLBY START -->
<library name="dap" path="libhwdapaidl.so"/>
<library name="dvl" path="libdlbvolaidl.so"/>
<!-- DOLBY SPATIALIZER -->
<library name="spatializer" path="libswspatializeraidl.so"/>
<!-- DOLBY GAME -->
<library name="gamedap" path="libswgamedapaidl.so"/>
<!-- DOLBY END -->
```
</details>

<details open>
<summary><strong>2. Effects (<code>&lt;effects&gt;</code>)</strong></summary>

```xml
<!-- DOLBY START -->
<effect name="dap" library="dap" uuid="9d4921da-8225-4f29-aefa-39537a04bcaa"/>
<effect name="dlb_music_listener" library="dvl" uuid="40f66c8b-5aa5-4345-8919-53ec431aaa98"/>
<effect name="dlb_ring_listener" library="dvl" uuid="21d14087-558a-4f21-94a9-5002dce64bce"/>
<effect name="dlb_alarm_listener" library="dvl" uuid="6aff229c-30c6-4cc8-9957-dbfe5c1bd7f6"/>
<!-- DOLBY SPATIALIZER -->
<effect name="spatializer" library="spatializer" uuid="ccd4cf09-a79d-46c2-9aae-06a1698d6c8f"/>
<!-- DOLBY GAME -->
<effect name="gamedap" library="gamedap" uuid="3783c334-d3a0-4d13-874f-0032e5fb80e2"/>
<!-- DOLBY END -->
```
</details>

<details open>
<summary><strong>3. Postprocess Streams (<code>&lt;postprocess&gt;</code>)</strong></summary>

```xml
    <postprocess>
        <stream type="music">
            <!-- <apply effect="music_helper"/> -->
            <apply effect="dlb_music_listener"/>
        </stream>
        <!-- <stream type="ring">
            <apply effect="ring_helper"/>
        </stream>
        <stream type="alarm">
            <apply effect="alarm_helper"/>
        </stream>
        <stream type="voice_call">
            <apply effect="voice_helper"/>
        </stream>
        <stream type="notification">
            <apply effect="notification_helper"/>
        </stream> -->
    </postprocess>
```
</details>

> **Tip:** Notice the library/effect names match cleanly (`name="dap" library="dap"`). Mismatched names like `library="dap_hw"` without a matching `<library>` tag will cause `audioserver` to drop the effect.

